code: 0
--- stdout
Use it to choose what to work on next: one line per open issue in the initial
status (statuses.initial) or without a status, in board order, leaving out
those with an unresolved blocker: open and not in a resolved status
(statuses.resolved), the rule of show and start. A blocker that is not on the
board, or that could not be read, counts as unresolved.

The blocked issues are counted; --all shows them too, with their blockers.
Filters combine with AND; the issues they leave out are counted. Only
issues are listed. gh dojo list shows the rest of the board.

Usage:
  gh dojo next [flags]

Examples:
  gh dojo next
  gh dojo next --mine --limit 1
  gh dojo next --label bug
  gh dojo next --sprint current
  gh dojo next --all

Flags:
      --all                 also show issues with unresolved blockers, naming them
  -h, --help                help for next
      --label stringArray   only issues with this label; repeat to require several
      --limit int           print at most this many issues (default 5)
      --mine                only issues assigned to you
      --sprint string       only issues in this sprint (fields.sprint): "current" (today, in board.timezone), a title, or "none"

Global Flags:
  -q, --jq expression       filter the JSON with a jq expression (implies --json)
      --json                print the result as JSON (schema_version 1), errors too
  -t, --template template   format the JSON with a Go template (implies --json)
--- stderr
